# QC Remote licensing

## Source-code license

Except for the material listed under "Material not covered by this license"
below, the source code and project documentation in this repository are
licensed, at your option, under either:

- the Apache License, Version 2.0 — see [`LICENSE-APACHE`](LICENSE-APACHE); or
- the MIT License — see [`LICENSE-MIT`](LICENSE-MIT).

The SPDX expression is `MIT OR Apache-2.0`.

Unless stated otherwise, contributions intentionally submitted for inclusion
in this project are licensed on the same terms. See
[`CONTRIBUTING.md`](CONTRIBUTING.md). Contributions must not add material of
the kinds described in "Device-derived and third-party-sourced material"
below unless the contribution also places it in a file listed in the
schedules in this file.

## Material not covered by this license

The `MIT OR Apache-2.0` grant above applies only to original work whose
copyright is held by Freevia EOOD ("Freevia") or by the contributors who
submitted it on the same terms. It does not apply to, and no license is
granted by Freevia for, the three categories below.

### Brand assets

The QC Remote name, wordmark, application icon, and derived platform icon sets
are not included in the open-source license grant and must be replaced in a
fork's public identity. See [`TRADEMARKS.md`](TRADEMARKS.md). They are:

- `packages/typescript/qc-theme/assets/app-icon.svg`
- `apps/windows/src-tauri/icons/**`
- `apps/android/android/app/src/main/res/mipmap-*/**`
- `apps/android/android/app/src/main/res/drawable-*/splash.png`
- the `appName`, `appWordmark`, and `companionCaption` values in
  `packages/typescript/qc-theme/src/brand.json`

### Third-party components

Third-party software and assets retain their own licenses and notices. The
repository's dependency notices and complete applicable license texts are in
[`THIRD_PARTY-NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY-NOTICES.md) and `legal/`. In-tree
third-party material includes:

- `packages/typescript/qc-theme/assets/fonts/*.ttf` — IBM Plex Sans, SIL Open
  Font License 1.1 (`packages/typescript/qc-theme/assets/fonts/LICENSE.txt`);
- protocol information incorporated from the `pyquadcortex` community project,
  MIT (`legal/COMMUNITY-PROTOCOL-LICENSE.txt`,
  `packages/rust/quadcortex/licenses/pyquadcortex-MIT.txt`);
- the Gradle Wrapper 8.14.3 — `apps/android/android/gradlew`,
  `apps/android/android/gradlew.bat`, and
  `apps/android/android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar` — Apache-2.0,
  copyright the original Gradle authors (unmodified; the JAR matches the
  SHA-256 Gradle publishes for that version);
- everything under `legal/`, which reproduces other parties' license texts.

### Device-derived and third-party-sourced material

Some files describe, measure, transcribe, or reconstruct the Neural DSP Quad
Cortex, its CorOS software, and Neural DSP's published documentation, so that
QC Remote can interoperate with the device. That material originates with
Neural DSP Technologies Oy or other third parties, not with Freevia.

That material is kept in whole files of its own. Each file is listed in
Schedule A or Schedule B below, by path or by a glob that matches whole
files, and is covered by the terms in
[`LICENSES/LicenseRef-QC-Remote-Reference.txt`](LICENSES/LicenseRef-QC-Remote-Reference.txt),
whose SPDX identifier is `LicenseRef-QC-Remote-Reference`. A package that
contains or embeds a listed file declares the SPDX expression
`(MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND LicenseRef-QC-Remote-Reference` in its metadata;
every other package declares `MIT OR Apache-2.0`. No file is covered only in
part: a file that is not listed is QC Remote's original work under
`MIT OR Apache-2.0`.

**Terms for this material, in summary.** It is provided for interoperability
and reference only. Freevia grants no license to Schedule A files and
claims no ownership of them; whatever rights subsist in them remain
with their respective owners. Schedule B files are licensed under
`MIT OR Apache-2.0` only to the extent of Freevia's own expression, and no
license is granted in Neural DSP's screen designs, user
interface, iconography, product design, or trade dress. Inclusion here is
not a statement that any owner has authorized the material. Whether a
particular use is permitted (for example under interoperability, quotation,
or fair-use provisions of applicable law) is for the person making the use
to determine. The material is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any
kind. The full terms are in `LICENSES/LicenseRef-QC-Remote-Reference.txt`.

#### Schedule A — device-derived and third-party-sourced files (no license granted)

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `docs/reference/qc-live-parameter-defaults.json` | Factory parameter defaults read from the device |
| `docs/reference/qc-live-parameter-scales.json` | Model catalogue read from the device: model names, categories, parameter names, ranges, scales, and option labels |
| `skills/qc-device-knowledge/references/data/qc-model-lineage.json` | Catalogue compiled from Neural DSP's device list, Quad Cortex User Manual 4.1.0, plugin pages, and CorOS release notes, including the third-party equipment names in its `based_on` fields |
| `skills/qc-device-knowledge/SKILL.md` | The device-knowledge skill, which quotes passages from Neural DSP documentation (marked by quotation marks and a `[MANUAL …]` or similar citation) alongside QC Remote's own explanatory text; listed whole |
| `packages/typescript/qc-ui/src/device-reference/**` | Text, names, values, and geometry transcribed from CorOS screens or Neural DSP documentation: on-screen and settings help copy, factory preset, capture, IR, model, and plugin names and their authors, the "Software information" values (Linux kernel, U-Boot, Zenjack, Zencoder, Zenwireless strings), the CorOS open-source license list, the device news QR matrix, glyph geometry traced from device screen frames or the manual, and the third-party application marks (Claude, ChatGPT, Antigravity, Bionic/LM Studio, Jan), which belong to their owners |
| `packages/typescript/qc-core/src/device-reference/**` | Parameter names, ranges, option labels (including factory IR names), and model-specific parameter orders as the device reports them; the demo preset with its model, capture, and plugin names; and the scene, preset-slot, block-category, and footswitch-lamp colour tables read from the device |
| `packages/typescript/qc-theme/src/screen-icon-vectors.ts` | Vector geometry traced from the device's screen frames |
| `packages/rust/quadcortex/src/device/native_library_seeds.rs` | Factory library folder and content names and keys |

Copies of these files produced or embedded by a build carry the same terms.
These include the two parameter catalogues copied into the Windows and
Android web bundles, and `SKILL.md` and `qc-model-lineage.json` compiled
into the Windows application and the `qc-remote-mcp` server.

#### Schedule B — screen reconstructions and device depictions (own expression only)

The files below reconstruct the layout, colours, and iconography of CorOS
screens, or depict Quad Cortex hardware, so that QC Remote's control surface
corresponds to the device it controls. They are licensed under
`MIT OR Apache-2.0` only to the extent of Freevia's own expression. **No
license is granted in Neural DSP's screen designs, user
interface, iconography, product design, or trade dress**, which these files
describe but which Freevia does not own.

